-- Machining - Thread Turning, Approach Length = 4. the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Threading sheet: the length of cut plus 4 mm
-- for the tool's approach and overrun (Threading!G16).
--
-- Machining - Knurling, TPI = 32. The knurl's threads per inch, from the drawing's knurl callout
-- (a pitch in mm is 25.4 / pitch TPI). With none on the drawing: the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx) Knurling sheet example, TPI 32 (Knurling!G11),
-- a feed of 25.4 / 32 = 0.794 mm/rev (G13 =25.4/G11).
--
-- Machining - Knurling, Cutting Speed = 6. the Machining calculator workbook (memory/Machining -
-- Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Knurling sheet: cutting speed 6 m/min (Knurling!G12).
--
-- Machining - Knurling, Passes = 4. the Machining calculator workbook (memory/Machining -
-- Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Knurling sheet: 4 passes (Knurling!G15).
--
-- Machining - Knurling, Max Spindle Speed. The selected machine's own top spindle speed
-- (mhr_records.specs spindle_speed_rpm, migration 1136, from memory/machining/machine). The
-- workbook has no cap; a machine cannot turn faster than its spindle.
--
-- Machining - Knurling, Approach Length = 4. the Machining calculator workbook (memory/Machining -
-- Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Knurling sheet: the length of cut plus 4 mm for the tool's
-- approach and overrun (Knurling!G16).
--
-- Machining - Step Drilling, Range Position = 0.3. 0.3: the median place of the workbook's worked
-- feeds inside the ranges the workbook gives for them (the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx); user decision 2026-11-25). Of 21 worked feeds
-- checked against the workbook's feed ranges, 15 fall inside, at Turning!G8 0, Slot Milling!G16 0,
-- Boring!F8 0.5, 0 and 0, Internal Boring!G13 0, End Milling and Sawing!I9 0.29, 1 and 0, Face
-- Milling!H8 0.29 and 1, Drilling!G12 0.5, Facing!G12 0.67, Step Drilling!G12 1, Plunge
-- Milling!G16 1: median 0.29. The worked depths of cut sit at 0 (3 of 3); the worked speeds fall
-- inside a range in only 14 of 36 checks. 0 takes a range's low end, 1 its high end.
--
-- Machining - Step Drilling, Max Spindle Speed. The selected machine's own top spindle speed
-- (mhr_records.specs spindle_speed_rpm, migration 1136). The workbook has no cap.
--
-- Machining - Step Drilling, Approach Length = 10. the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Step Drilling sheet: the length of cut plus
-- 10 mm for the tool's approach and overrun (Step Drilling!G14).
--
-- Machining - Internal Boring, Depth of Cut = 0.5. the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Internal Boring sheet: depth of cut 0.5 mm
-- (Internal Boring!G14).
--
-- Machining - Internal Boring, Range Position = 0.3. 0.3: the median place of the workbook's
-- worked feeds inside the ranges the workbook gives for them (the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx); user decision 2026-11-25). Of 21 worked feeds
-- checked against the workbook's feed ranges, 15 fall inside, at Turning!G8 0, Slot Milling!G16 0,
-- Boring!F8 0.5, 0 and 0, Internal Boring!G13 0, End Milling and Sawing!I9 0.29, 1 and 0, Face
-- Milling!H8 0.29 and 1, Drilling!G12 0.5, Facing!G12 0.67, Step Drilling!G12 1, Plunge
-- Milling!G16 1: median 0.29. The worked depths of cut sit at 0 (3 of 3); the worked speeds fall
-- inside a range in only 14 of 36 checks. 0 takes a range's low end, 1 its high end.
--
-- Machining - Internal Boring, Max Spindle Speed. The selected machine's own top spindle speed
-- (mhr_records.specs spindle_speed_rpm, migration 1136). The workbook has no cap.
--
-- Machining - Internal Boring, Approach Length = 4. the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Internal Boring sheet: the length of cut plus
-- 4 mm for the tool's approach and overrun (Internal Boring!G17).
--
-- Machining - Boring, Depth of Cut = 0.5. the Machining calculator workbook (memory/Machining -
-- Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Internal Boring sheet: depth of cut 0.5 mm (Internal Boring!G14).
--
-- Machining - Boring, Range Position = 0.3. 0.3: the median place of the workbook's worked feeds
