-- Calculator Database (1).xlsx), Internal Boring sheet: the length of cut plus 4 mm for the tool's
-- approach and overrun (Internal Boring!G17).
--
-- Machining - Plunge Milling, Range Position = 0.3. 0.3: the median place of the workbook's worked
-- feeds inside the ranges the workbook gives for them (the Machining calculator workbook
-- (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx); user decision 2026-11-25). Of 21 worked feeds
-- checked against the workbook's feed ranges, 15 fall inside, at Turning!G8 0, Slot Milling!G16 0,
-- Boring!F8 0.5, 0 and 0, Internal Boring!G13 0, End Milling and Sawing!I9 0.29, 1 and 0, Face
-- Milling!H8 0.29 and 1, Drilling!G12 0.5, Facing!G12 0.67, Step Drilling!G12 1, Plunge
-- Milling!G16 1: median 0.29. The worked depths of cut sit at 0 (3 of 3); the worked speeds fall
