    RETURNING id INTO v_id;
  ELSE
    UPDATE public.calculators SET description = $q$Chamfering edges, timed as the Machining calculator workbook (memory/Machining - Calculator Database (1).xlsx) times an end mill (its End Milling sheet): one pass along each edge, n = 1000 v / (pi D) at the cutter's diameter capped at the machine's spindle limit, time = (edge length + 10 mm + D / 2) / (feed per tooth x teeth x n), rounded up to whole seconds an edge. The speed and feed per tooth are the workbook's milling ones for the material (tblMillingConditions); the cutter is the material's end mill (tblMillingFinishing). An edge's length is the CAD's: pi x its diameter for a round edge, else the edge face's longest extent (its length on a straight edge; a curved one reads shorter). Was the edge length at the tblChamfering edge speed, and a set 5 s for an edge with no CAD size (user decision 2026-11-25).$q$, updated_at = now() WHERE id = v_id;
